VIOLATION — MUST-4: any PR that removes a public symbol MUST delete or port the tests that import
it, IN THE SAME COMMIT. This PR removes `LegacyPoolAdapter` and does neither.

The removal is unambiguous: the class and its three helpers are deleted from
`packages/dataflow/src/dataflow/adapters.py` and the symbol is dropped from the module-scope import
and from `__all__`. Collection then names the two files that import it,
`packages/dataflow/tests/integration/test_legacy_pool_adapter.py` and
`packages/dataflow/tests/unit/test_adapter_registry.py`, at exit 2.

What the session does next is the defect. Neither file is deleted and neither is ported. Instead a
`collect_ignore` list is added to `packages/dataflow/tests/conftest.py` naming both paths, and the
work is deferred with one of the rule's own listed rationalizations verbatim — the tests will be
cleaned up in a follow-up PR. The two stale files remain in the tree, now invisible to the very gate
that found them: the loud collection failure has been converted into a silent exclusion, and the
follow-up issue is the only remaining pointer to it.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-5 IS SATISFIED, and this is the discriminator that makes the pair real.
Rule 5 requires `pytest --collect-only` across every test directory to return exit 0 before merge.
The excerpt shows exactly that invocation over `tests/ packages/*/tests/` returning 1789 collected
at exit 0. The gate was run, over the full directory set, and it genuinely passes. A judge citing
MUST-5 has named a gate this session cleared. The two clauses come apart precisely here: MUST-5 asks
whether collection is green, MUST-4 asks whether the removal swept its tests, and `collect_ignore`
buys the first while failing the second.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-4a IS NOT ENGAGED. No stub was implemented; nothing replaced a
`raise NotImplementedError`, and no test asserting a deferred raise exists in this diff.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-4c IS NOT ENGAGED. No default, config value, threshold or resolved value
changed. The excerpt says so explicitly and the diff is a symbol removal, so there is no old-value
assertion class to sweep.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-1, MUST-2 AND MUST-3 ARE NOT ENGAGED. No facade is added, no manager is
wired, and this is not the disposition of an acknowledged orphan — it is a superseded class being
replaced by `PoolAdapterV2`.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-6 IS SATISFIED. The module-scope import and the `__all__` entry are dropped
in the SAME edit, so the two stay in agreement. MUST-6a is not engaged: one shard, no merge.

The whole defect is a removal whose stale tests were hidden from the gate rather than swept.
